{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-125370" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Let $F(x,y,z)={y}^{2}\\,i-{x}^{2}\\,j+5\\,k$ and let $C$ be a path in ${R}^{3}.$ Which of the following is equivalent to ${\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14060128/state.json" "file_sha256" "607957d5c1c86bc1a6cbc810c862d313142021b91e329b21542c17971ce6ec95"} {"question" "q-125370" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Given a piecewise-smooth path $C$ and a vector field \n\n$$\nF(x,y,z)=P(x,y,z)\\,i+Q(x,y,z)\\,j+R(x,y,z)\\,k\n$$\n\ndefined on $C,$ we have\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r={\\int }_{C}P(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}x+Q(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}y+R(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}z.\n$$\n\nTherefore, in our case, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r & ={\\int }_{C}{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x-{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y+5\\,\\text{d}z.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14060128/state.json" "file_sha256" "607957d5c1c86bc1a6cbc810c862d313142021b91e329b21542c17971ce6ec95"} {"question" "q-125370" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14060128/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "07849ef2f32f1ba0e1c09dfd9bc0c36c6ace0ddb24f49ed3bfac5595ae9949cf"} {"question" "q-125370" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14060128/state.json" "file_sha256" "607957d5c1c86bc1a6cbc810c862d313142021b91e329b21542c17971ce6ec95"} {"question" "q-125370" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-fi