142021b91e329b21542c17971ce6ec95"} {"question" "q-39342" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We will use the fact that\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r={\\int }_{{C}_{1}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r+{\\int }_{{C}_{2}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r.\n$$\n\nWe're given the value of the first integral, so we only need to work out the second.\n\nThe path ${C}_{2}$ is the line segment from $A$ to $B.$ It can be parametrized as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{2}(t) & =a+t(b-a) \\\\  & =⟨2,0⟩+t(⟨1,1⟩-⟨2,0⟩) \\\\  & =⟨2-t,t⟩ \\\\  & =(2-t)\\,i+t\\,j,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $0<t<1.$ Along this segment, we have $x=2-t$ and $y=t.$ Therefore, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F({r}_{2}(t)) & =(x+y)\\,i+(x-y)\\,j \\\\  & =(2-t+t)\\,i+(2-t-t)\\,j \\\\  & =2\\,i+(2-2t)\\,j.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComputing the derivative, we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{2}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2-t)i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t)j \\\\  & =-i+j\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now compute the dot product:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F({r}_{2}(t))\\cdot {r}_{2}^{′}(t) & =(2\\,i+(2-2t)\\,j)\\cdot (-i+j) \\\\  & =-2+(2-2t) \\\\  & =-2t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we can evaluate the integral, as follows: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r & ={\\int }_{{C}_{1}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r+{\\int }_{{C}_{2}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r \\\\  & =2+{\\int }_{0}^{1}F({r}_{2}(t))\\cdot {r}_{2}^{′}(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =2+{\\int }_{0}^{1}(-2t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =2-{t}^{2}{|}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =2-(1-0) \\\\  & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14060128/state.json" "file_sha256" "607957d5c1c86bc1a6cbc810c862d313142021b91e329b21542c17971ce6ec95"} {"question" "q-39342" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14060128/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "07849ef2f32f1ba0e1c09dfd9bc0c36c6ace0ddb24f49ed3bfac5595ae9949cf"} {"question" "q-39342" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14060128/state.json" "file_sha256" "607957d5c1c86bc1a6cbc810c862d313142021b91e329b21542c17971ce6ec95"} {"question" "q-39342" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "1"] ["math" "2"] ["math" "3"] ["math" "4"] ["math" "6"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14060128/state.json" "file_sha256" "607957d5c1c86bc1a6cbc810c862d313142021b91e329b21542c17971ce6ec95"} {"question" "q-39342" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "1"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14060128/state.json" "file_sha256" "607957d5c1c86bc1a6cbc810c862d313142021b91e329b21542c17971ce6ec95"} {"question" "q-77191" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14060128/assets/0457cb819e6f39ef9c0978e356cff788e1cf5edbef9cbf844a054ab777b70eac.png)\n\nThe path ${C}_{1}$ consists of a the line segment from the point $A(-2,0)$ to the point $B(0,1),$ and the path ${C}_{2}$ consists of the line segment from the point $B(0,1)$ to the point $D(1,1).$\n\nGiven that ${\\int }_{{C}_{2}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r=-\\frac{3}{2},$ evaluate ${\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r,$ where $F(x,y)=(x-2y)\\,i+(y-x)\\,j,$ and $C={C}_{1}\\cup {C}_{2}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14060128/state.json" "file_sha256" "607957d5c1c86bc1a6cbc810c862d313142021b91e329b21542c17971ce6ec95"} {"question" "q-77191" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We will use the fact that\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r={\\int }_{{C}_{1}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r+{\\int }_{{C}_{2}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r.\n$$\n\nWe're given the value of the second integral, so we only need to work out the first.\n\nThe path ${C}_{1}$ is the line segment from $A$ to $B.$  It can be parametrized as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{1}(t) & =a+t(b-a) \\\\  & =⟨-2,0⟩+t(⟨0,1⟩-⟨-2,0⟩) \\\\  & =⟨-2+2t,t⟩ \\\\  & =(-2+2t)i+t\\,j,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $0<t<1.$ Along this segment, we have $x=-2+2t$ and $y=t.$ Therefore, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F({r}_{1}(t)) & =(x-2y)\\,i+(y-x)\\,j \\\\  & =((-2+2t)-2t)\\,i+(t-(-2+2t))\\,j \\\\  & =-2\\,i+(2-t)\\,j.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComputing the derivative, we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{1}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(-2+2t)i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t)j \\\\  & =2\\,i+j\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now compute the dot product:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F({r}_{1}(t))\\cdot {r}_{1}^{′}(t) & =(-2\\,i+(2-t)\\,j)\\cdot (2\\,i+j) \\\\  & =-2-t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we can evaluate the integral, as follows: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r & ={\\int }_{{C}_{1}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r+{\\int }_{{C}_{2}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}F({r}_{1}(t))\\cdot {r}_{1}^{′}(t)\\,\\text{d}t+(-\\frac{3}{2}) \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}(-2-t)\\,\\text{d}t-\\frac{3}{2} \\\\  & ={[-2t-\\frac{{t}^{2}}{2}]}_{0}^{1}-\\frac{3}{2} \\\\  & =[-2(1)-\\frac{{1}^{2}}{2}-0]-\\frac{3}{2} \\\\  & =-\\frac{5}{2}-\\frac{3}{2} \\\\  & =-4\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14060128/state.json" "file_sha256" "607957d5c1c86bc1a6cbc810c862d313142021b91e329b21542c17971ce6ec95"} {"question" "q-77191" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14060128/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "07849ef2f32f1ba0e1c09dfd9bc0c36c6ace0ddb24f49ed3bfac5595ae9949cf"} {"question" "q-77191" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14060128/state.json" "file_sha256" "607957d5c1c86bc1a6cbc810c862d313142021b91e329b21542c17971ce6ec95"} {"question" "q-77191" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-4"] ["math" "-\\frac{3}{2}"] ["math" "4"] ["math" "5"] ["math" "\\frac{3}{2}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14060128/state.json" "file_sha256" "607957d5c1c86bc1a6cbc810c862d313142021b91e329b21542c17971ce6ec95"} {"question" "q-77191" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-4"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14060128/state.json" "file_sha256" "607957d5c1c86bc1a6cbc810c862d313142021b91e329b21542c17971ce6ec95"} {"question" "q-39673" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14060128/assets/73c6a8268a179f72611fb65e099d1249d48501e4fd4731d03747800e1944fd97.png)\n\nThe path ${C}_{1}$ consists of a the line segment from the point $A(0,1)$ to the point $B(1,2),$ and the path ${C}_{2}$ consists of a line segment from the point $B(1,2)$ to the point $D(1,3).$\n\nGiven that ${\\int }_{{C}_{2}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r=\\frac{7}{2},$ evaluate ${\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r,$ where $F(x,y)=(2x-3y)\\,i+(x+y)\\,j,$ and $C={C}_{1}\\cup {C}_{2}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14060128/state.json" "file_sha256" "607957d5c1c86bc1a6cbc810c862d313142021b91e329b21542c17971ce6ec95"} {"question" "q-39673" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We will use the fact that\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r={\\int }_{{C}_{1}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r+{\\int }_{{C}_{2}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r.\n$$\n\nWe're given the value of the second integral, so we only need to work out the first.\n\nThe path ${C}_{1}$ is the line segment from $A$ to $B.$  It can be parametrized as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{1}(t) & =a+t(b-a) \\\\  & =⟨0,1⟩+t(⟨1,2⟩-⟨0,1⟩) \\\\  & =⟨t,1+t⟩ \\\\  & =t\\,i+(1+t)\\,j,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $0<t<1.$ Along this segment, we have $x=t$ and $y=1+t.$ Therefore, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F({r}_{1}(t)) & =(2x-3y)\\,i+(x+y)\\,j \\\\  & =(2t-3(1+t))\\,i+(t+(1+t))\\,j \\\\  & =(-3-t)\\,i+(2t+1)\\,j.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComputing the derivative, we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{1}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t)i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(1+t)j \\\\  & =i+j\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now compute the dot product:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F({r}_{1}(t))\\cdot {r}_{1}^{′}(t) & =((-3-t)\\,i+(2t+1)\\,j)\\cdot (i+j) \\\\  & =-3-t+2t+1 \\\\  & =t-2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we can evaluate the integral, as follows: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r & ={\\int }_{{C}_{1}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r+{\\int }_{{C}_{2}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}F({r}_{1}(t))\\cdot {r}_{1}^{′}(t)\\,\\text{d}t+\\frac{7}{2} \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}(t-2)\\,\\text{d}t+\\frac{7}{2} \\\\  & ={[\\frac{{t}^{2}}{2}-2t]}_{0}^{1}+\\frac{7}{2} \\\\  & =[\\frac{1}{2}-2-0]+\\frac{7}{2} \\\\  & =-\\frac{3}{2}+\\frac{7}{2} \\\\  & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14060128/state.json" "file_sha256" "607957d5c1c86bc1a6cbc810c862d313142021b91e329b21542c17971ce6ec95"} {"question" "q-39673" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14060128/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "07849ef2f32f1ba0e1c09dfd9bc0c36c6ace0ddb24f49ed3bfac5595ae9949cf"} {"question" "q-39673" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14060128/state.json" "file_sha256" "607957d5c1c86bc1a6cbc810c862d313142021b91e329b21542c17971ce6ec95"} {"question" "q-39673" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-\\frac{3}{2}"] ["math" "2"] ["math" "2+\\operatorname{ln}⁡3"] ["math" "\\frac{7}{2}"] ["math" "e-2"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14060128/state.json" "file_sha256" "607957d5c1c86bc1a6cbc810c862d313142021b91e329b21542c17971ce6ec95"} {"question" "q-39673" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "2"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14060128/state.json" "file_sha256" "607957d5c1c86bc1a6cbc810c862d313142021b91e329b21542c17971ce6ec95"} {"question" "q-77180" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14060128/assets/93c6184f39b28a057866bb02e11e5e81a7abea4ff8a9a907670dd30cfc93d557.png)\n\nThe path ${C}_{1}$ consists of a line segment from the point $A(1,-1)$ to the point $B(1,1),$ and the path ${C}_{2}$ consists of a line segment from the point $B(1,1)$ to the point $O(0,0).$\n\nGiven that ${\\int }_{{C}_{1}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r=2,$ evaluate ${\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r,$ where $F(x,y)=(2x+y)\\,i+(x-2y)\\,j,$ and $C={C}_{1}\\cup {C}_{2}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14060128/state.json" "file_sha256" "607957d5c1c86bc1a6cbc810c862d313142021b91e329b21542c17971ce6ec95"} {"question" "q-77180" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We will use the fact that\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r={\\int }_{{C}_{1}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r+{\\int }_{{C}_{2}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r.\n$$\n\nWe're given the value of the first integral, so we only need to work out the second.\n\nThe path ${C}_{2}$ is the line segment from $B$ to $O.$ It can be parametrized as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{2}(t) & =b+t(0-b) \\\\  & =⟨1,1⟩+t(⟨0,0⟩-⟨1,1⟩) \\\\  & =⟨1-t,1-t⟩ \\\\  & =(1-t)\\,i+(1-t)\\,j,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $0<t<1.$ Along this segment, we have $x=1-t$ and $y=1-t.$ Therefore, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F({r}_{2}(t)) & =(2x+y)\\,i+(x-2y)\\,j \\\\  & =(2(1-t)+(1-t))\\,i+((1-t)-2(1-t))\\,j \\\\  & =(3-3t)\\,i+(-1+t)\\,j.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComputing the derivative, we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{2}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(1-t)i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(1-t)j \\\\  & =-i-j\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now compute the dot product:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F({r}_{2}(t))\\cdot {r}_{2}^{′}(t) & =((3-3t)\\,i+(-1+t)\\,j)\\cdot (-i-j) \\\\  & =-3+3t+1-t \\\\  & =-2+2t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we can evaluate the integral, as follows: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r & ={\\int }_{{C}_{1}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r+{\\int }_{{C}_{2}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r \\\\  & =2+{\\int }_{0}^{1}F({r}_{2}(t))\\cdot {r}_{2}^{′}(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =2+{\\int }_{0}^{1}(-2+2t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =2+(-2t+{t}^{2})\\,{|}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =2+(1-2) \\\\  & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14060128/state.json" "file_sha256" "607957d5c1c86bc1a6cbc810c862d313142021b91e329b21542c17971ce6ec95"} {"question" "q-77180" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14060128/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "07849ef2f32f1ba0e1c09dfd9bc0c36c6ace0ddb24f49ed3bfac5595ae9949cf"} {"question" "q-77180" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14060128/state.json" "file_sha256" "607957d5c1c86bc1a6cbc810c862d313142021b91e329b21542c17971ce6ec95"} {"question" "q-77180" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-1"] ["math" "-4"] ["math" "1"] ["math" "3"] ["math" "5"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14060128/state.json" "file_sha256" "607957d5c1c86bc1a6cbc810c862d313142021b91e329b21542c17971ce6ec95"} {"question" "q-77180" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "1"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14060128/state.json" "file_sha256" "607957d5c1c86bc1a6cbc810c862d313142021b91e329b21542c17971ce6ec95"} {"question" "q-39674" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14060128/assets/512905447203d1d3a96781d20d586f9c4cf5cc9392fab50607b6fc77e9b00121.png)\n\nThe path ${C}_{1}$ consists of a section of the parabola $y={x}^{2}$ from the point $O(0,0)$ to the point $A(2,4),$ and the path ${C}_{2}$ consists of a line segment from the point $A(2,4)$ to the point $B(0,4).$\n\nGiven that ${\\int }_{{C}_{2}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r=-2,$ evaluate ${\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r,$ where $F(x,y)=x\\,i+y\\,j$ and $C={C}_{1}\\cup {C}_{2}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14060128/state.json" "file_sha256" "607957d5c1c86bc1a6cbc810c862d313142021b91e329b21542c17971ce6ec95"} {"question" "q-39674" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We will use the fact that\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r={\\int }_{{C}_{1}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r+{\\int }_{{C}_{2}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r.\n$$\n\nWe're given the value of the second integral, so we only need to work out the first.\n\n${C}_{1}$ is the section of parabola $y={x}^{2}$ from $O$ to $A.$ It can be parametrized as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{1}(t)=t\\,i+{t}^{2}\\,j,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $0<t<2.$ Along this curve, we have $x=t$ and $y={t}^{2}.$ Therefore, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F({r}_{1}(t)) & =x\\,i+y\\,j \\\\  & =t\\,i+{t}^{2}\\,j.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComputing the derivative, we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{1}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t)i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{2})j \\\\  & =i+2t\\,j\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now compute the dot product:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F({r}_{1}(t))\\cdot {r}_{1}^{′}(t) & =(t\\,i+{t}^{2}\\,j)\\cdot (i+2t\\,j) \\\\  & =t+2{t}^{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we can evaluate the integral, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r & ={\\int }_{{C}_{1}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r+{\\int }_{{C}_{2}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}F({r}_{1}(t))\\cdot {r}_{1}^{′}(t)\\,\\text{d}t-2 \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}(t+2{t}^{3})\\,\\text{d}t-2 \\\\  & ={[\\frac{{t}^{2}}{2}+\\frac{{t}^{4}}{2}]}_{0}^{2}-2 \\\\  & =[2+8]-2 \\\\  & =10-2 \\\\  & =8\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14060128/state.json" "file_sha256" "607957d5c1c86bc1a6cbc810c862d313142021b91e329b21542c17971ce6ec95"} {"question" "q-39674" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14060128/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "07849ef2f32f1ba0e1c09dfd9bc0c36c6ace0ddb24f49ed3bfac5595ae9949cf"} {"question" "q-39674" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14060128/state.json" "file_sha256" "607957d5c1c86bc1a6cbc810c862d313142021b91e329b21542c17971ce6ec95"} {"question" "q-39674" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-2"] ["math" "0"] ["math" "10"] ["math" "2"] ["math" "8"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14060128/state.json" "file_sha256" "607957d5c1c86bc1a6cbc810c862d313142021b91e329b21542c17971ce6ec95"} {"question" "q-39674" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "8"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14060128/state.json" "file_sha256" "607957d5c1c86bc1a6cbc810c862d313142021b91e329b21542c17971ce6ec95"} {"question" "e-9535" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Let $\\mathbf{F}(x,y) = (3x+2) \\: \\mathbf{i} - y^3 \\: \\mathbf{j}$ and let $C$ be a path in $\\mathbb R^2.$ Write $\\displaystyle \\int\\limits_C \\mathbf{F} \\cdot \\text{d}\\mathbf{r}$ in the form $\\displaystyle\\int_C P(x,y)\\,\\textrm d x +  Q(x,y)\\,\\textrm d y.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14060128/example-9535.json" "file_sha256" "2a3d26811d5fecd2a2368e205028c8687c224604a11e98653976a5026e42cdc1"} {"question" "e-9535" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Given a piecewise-smooth path $C$ and a vector field \n\n$$\n\\mathbf{F}(x,y) = P(x,y) \\: \\mathbf{i} + Q(x,y) \\: \\mathbf{j}\n$$\n\ndefined on $C,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\int\\limits_C \\mathbf{F} \\cdot \\text{d}\\mathbf{r} = \\int\\limits_C P(x,y) \\: \\text{d}x + Q(x,y) \\: \\text{d}y.\n$$\n\nIn our case, $P = 3x+2$ and $Q = -y^3.$ Therefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r & ={\\int }_{C}(3x+2)\\,\\text{d}x-{y}^{3}\\,\\text{d}y.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14060128/example-9535.json" "file_sha256" "2a3d26811d5fecd2a2368e205028c8687c224604a11e98653976a5026e42cdc1"} {"question" "e-6319" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14060128/assets/38ab4af726729b5c9804f4aa13801d637e5e62eda085d6611174586827ef8c11.png)\n\nConsider the integral $\\displaystyle \\int\\limits_{C} \\mathbf{F} \\cdot \\textrm{d}\\mathbf{r},$ where $C$ is the closed polygonal path $FGHF$ shown above, traversed in the **clockwise** direction. Express this integral as a sum of line integrals along $C_1, C_2,$ and $C_3.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14060128/example-6319.json" "file_sha256" "edcf0b9c29872d77e75a5027969c5b69efc3f90ef374d7839b68c035cae1de0d"} {"question" "e-6319" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, notice that we can represent $C,$ which is traversed in clockwise, as the union of $3$ paths:\n\n$$\nC = \\{-C_1\\} \\cup \\{-C_2\\} \\cup C_3,\n$$\n\nwhere $-C_1$ and $-C_2$ are the same paths as $C_1$ and $C_2$ but traversed in the opposite direction.\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r & ={\\int }_{-{C}_{1}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r+{\\int }_{-{C}_{2}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r+{\\int }_{{C}_{3}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r \\\\  & =-{\\int }_{{C}_{1}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r-{\\int }_{{C}_{2}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r+{\\int }_{{C}_{3}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14060128/example-6319.json" "file_sha256" "edcf0b9c29872d77e75a5027969c5b69efc3f90ef374d7839b68c035cae1de0d"} {"question" "e-6286" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14060128/assets/001487e4a94988a24d15702a18692e9deb2495a7cc7ec5c9f71b98fea13e0ce8.png)\n\nThe path $C_1$ consists of a line segment from the point $A(-2,0)$ to the point $O(0,0),$ and the path $C_2$ consists of a line segment from the point $O(0,0)$ to the point $B(1,1).$\n\nGiven that $\\displaystyle \\int\\limits_{C_1} \\mathbf{F} \\cdot \\textrm{d}\\mathbf{r} = -4,$ evaluate $\\displaystyle \\int\\limits_{C} \\mathbf{F} \\cdot \\textrm{d}\\mathbf{r},$ where $\\mathbf{F}(x, y) = (2x-3y) \\,\\mathbf{i} + (2y-5x)\\,\\mathbf {j}$ and $C = C_1\\cup C_2.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14060128/example-6286.json" "file_sha256" "69c31980fa23cc55203f1baf7499c3fdff9d784d03328c51691cf60d65e5b1f7"} {"question" "e-6286" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We will use the fact that\n\n$$\n\\int\\limits_{C} \\mathbf{F} \\cdot \\textrm{d}\\mathbf{r} = \\int\\limits_{C_1} \\mathbf{F} \\cdot \\textrm{d}\\mathbf{r}\n+\n \\int\\limits_{C_2} \\mathbf{F} \\cdot \\textrm{d}\\mathbf{r}.\n$$\n\nWe're given the value of the first integral, so we only need to work out the second.\n\nThe path $C_2$ is the line segment from $O$ to $B.$ It can be parametrized as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{2}(t) & =b+t(c-b) \\\\  & =⟨0,0⟩+t(⟨1,1⟩-⟨0,0⟩) \\\\  & =⟨t,t⟩ \\\\  & =t\\,i+t\\,j,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $0 \\lt t \\lt 1.$ Along this segment, we have $x = t$ and $y = t.$ Therefore, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F({r}_{2}(t)) & =(2x-3y)\\,i+(2y-5x)\\,j \\\\  & =(2t-3t)\\,i+(2t-5t)\\,j \\\\  & =-t\\,i-3t\\,j.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComputing the derivative, we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{2}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t)i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t)j \\\\  & =i+j\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now compute the dot product:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F({r}_{2}(t))\\cdot {r}_{2}^{′}(t) & =(-t\\,i-3t\\,j)\\cdot (i+j) \\\\  & =-t\\cdot 1+(-3t)\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =-4t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we can evaluate the integral, as follows: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r & ={\\int }_{{C}_{1}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r+{\\int }_{{C}_{2}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r \\\\  & =-4+{\\int }_{0}^{1}F({r}_{2}(t))\\cdot {r}_{2}^{′}(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =-4+{\\int }_{0}^{1}(-4t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =-4+[-2{t}^{2}]_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =-4+[-2+0] \\\\  & =-6\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14060128/example-6286.json" "file_sha256" "69c31980fa23cc55203f1baf7499c3fdff9d784d03328c51691cf60d65e5b1f7"} {"question" "q-125370" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "{\\int }_{C}{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x-{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y+5\\,\\text{d}z"] "category" "reviewed_ma_solution" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14060128/answer-source-reviews.json" "file_sha256" "42aac9c5926eb866ad60ce087080b964e8ccffdb5f5e873390abce61f100b1d3" "reviewer_session" "01a11908-fa8d-7c61-8e03-c1185d0b9506" "rationale" "Since F=(y²,-x²,5) and dr=(dx,dy,dz), their dot product is y²dx−x²dy+5dz, integrated over C. This is original option a and matches the authentic worked solution and stored key, preserving the integral's scope over all three terms. Saved grading rejected the submitted option b; this is a derived judgment, not a successful grade for option a." "bindings" {"problem" "f1ba5f1a00dbea50752d82243b193297cc58bb906819383794ad4f9eb12c4636" "worked_solution" "3a2c4f4e18c26b85150513e052740f80c08e8faa669976f29086f09aaeacc11c" "original_field" "b773da15239cd3033f3da1c0c0bc5577c10311518c6ae7b8c4819bba3788b13f" "reviewed_field" "8716eb8cfa37afa297cf3c2898d039e56a66ea3b04a8d38338e430d642495372" "raw_widget" "7e6ea32bd9e4514160b7ad88ded6d78b3536f81639f9c7ee738a68581094e8da"} "evidence_files" [{"path" "q-125370-before.png" "sha256" "8417cfd83d1a638cbdd2cdd14d9736acd56dbff1d2b276f588c0680f0774d63c"} {"path" "history-q-125370.png" "sha256" "b607e663c34cdaebb6d32db1620a7d6dead73cb91b7609a9ca0320890ba8579e"} {"path" "q-125370-after.json" "sha256" "22fd2689edc54e0b968ebbf2ee9f72ecfb29122a4c238b75691501b0635b785a"} {"path" "edb-import/questions.edn" "sha256" "5024a859e6f7811eb5c0e2e5727f27584a7638cbf32b9e940188591a56201a59"}]} {"question" "q-125370" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "{\\int }_{C}({y}^{2}+{x}^{2}+5)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}z"] ["math" "{\\int }_{C}({y}^{2}-{x}^{2})\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y+5\\,\\text{d}z"] ["math" "{\\int }_{C}{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x-{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y+5\\,\\text{d}z"] ["math" "{\\int }_{C}{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x+{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y"] ["math" "{\\int }_{C}{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x-{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y+5\\,\\text{d}z"]] "category" "reviewed_ma_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14060128/answer-source-reviews.json" "file_sha2